caption: Mastery Requirements
tradition-component: mastery-requirements

Both Revelator Talents at 4.

Will 20.

At least three materially distinct permanent Conjunction Abilities purchased and used during consequential play, each representing a different interaction between the two Revelator Powers.

Use Wild Branch Manifestation during consequential play to manifest at least one Advanced ability belonging solely to each Revelator Power.

At least 100 character points total invested after modifiers in Revelator traits. Abilities purchased under the two Revelator Talents' Basic branch access and permanent Conjunction Abilities count. Temporary Wild Ability manifestations and unrelated traits do not. Attributes and Talents do not count toward this investment.

Complete a consequential deed in which a purchased Conjunction Ability succeeds specifically because both Revelator Powers contribute to the result.

Complete the requirement for the chosen Path:

The Whole Truth: make at least three consequential rolls on materially distinct Conjunction Abilities that benefit from both Revelator Talents through Whole Truth.

The Living Truth: successfully graft at least three materially distinct temporary abilities onto purchased Conjunction Abilities and use the resulting conjunctions consequentially.

The Shared Truth: successfully use at least three materially distinct Shared Techniques during consequential play, each affecting at least two components of a purchased Conjunction Ability.
